Create libstdc++'s thread-atexit key at library initialization, before any
TLS access can create emutls' key, so that it sorts first; keep the
std::atexit registration lazy.  Runtime library only (libstdc++.6.dylib and
the static libstdc++/libsupc++), no compiler change.

Background: thread_local destructors ran on storage libgcc's emutls had already freed:
GCC on Darwin has no native TLS, thread_local is emutls, whose per-thread
blocks a pthread key destructor (emutls_destroy) releases; libstdc++ has no
__cxa_thread_atexit_impl on Darwin and runs the C++ thread_local destructors
from a pthread key of its own, created lazily on the first __cxa_thread_atexit
call, i.e. always after emutls created its key, and _pthread_tsd_cleanup runs
key destructors in key order.  Seen as node 24 (V8 13.6, absl::Mutex-backed
base::Mutex) dying with EXC_BAD_INSTRUCTION at every V8 worker-thread exit:
the unique_ptr holder of abseil's ThreadIdentity was destroyed on a freed
block, the deleter slot holding malloc's free-list link.

--- libstdc++-v3/libsupc++/atexit_thread.cc
+++ libstdc++-v3/libsupc++/atexit_thread.cc
@@ -123,14 +123,33 @@
     run (e);
   }
 
-  // Initialize the key for the cleanup stack.  We use a static local for
-  // key init/delete rather than atexit so that delete is run on dlclose.
+  // Create the key for the cleanup stack.  We use an object for key
+  // create/delete rather than atexit so that delete is run on dlclose.
+  //
+  // The key is created at library initialization, not on the first
+  // __cxa_thread_atexit call: with emulated TLS (libgcc's emutls) the
+  // thread_local objects live in storage that a gthread key destructor of
+  // its own releases, POSIX implementations such as Darwin's run key
+  // destructors in key creation order, and the first __cxa_thread_atexit
+  // call is always preceded by a TLS access (the object's address).  A key
+  // created lazily therefore sorts after emutls' and the destructors run
+  // on freed storage.  The std::atexit registration stays lazy so that the
+  // main thread's thread_local destructors keep running before the static
+  // destructors registered after them.
+  struct key_s {
+    bool created;
+    key_s() : created(false) { create(); }
+    ~key_s() { if (created) __gthread_key_delete (key); }
+    void create() {
+      if (!created && __gthread_active_p ()
+	  && __gthread_key_create (&key, run) == 0)
+	created = true;
+    }
+  };
+  key_s ks;
+
   void key_init() {
-    struct key_s {
-      key_s() { __gthread_key_create (&key, run); }
-      ~key_s() { __gthread_key_delete (key); }
-    };
-    static key_s ks;
+    ks.create();
     // Also make sure the destructors are run by std::exit.
     // FIXME TLS cleanups should run before static cleanups and atexit
     // cleanups.
